<https://w3id.org/cerise-see/examples/pv-lci#scenario-activity-water-deionised-water-balance-according-to-moek-2013-at-plant-cn> dcterms:description "ADDED BACKGROUND SCENARIO, not an Excel worksheet. Assume 1000 kg water/m3, EUR 2/m3 for water supply and 0.005 MJ electricity/kg for deionisation. Thus 1 kg requires EUR 0.002 water service and 0.005 MJ electricity. The German monetary water sector is a geographic proxy for Chinese water because the Chinese offering has no published provider URI; Chinese electricity is used. Resins, chemicals and treatment infrastructure are not separately modelled. These are illustrative coefficients, not plant data." .
<https://w3id.org/cerise-see/examples/pv-lci#scenario-background-water-deionised-water-balance-according-to-moek-2013-at-plant-cn-m-electricity> dcterms:description "Scenario coefficient per one kg of water, deionised, water balance according to MoeK 2013, at plant. Assume 1000 kg water/m3, EUR 2/m3 for water supply and 0.005 MJ electricity/kg for deionisation. Thus 1 kg requires EUR 0.002 water service and 0.005 MJ electricity. The German monetary water sector is a geographic proxy for Chinese water because the Chinese offering has no published provider URI; Chinese electricity is used. Resins, chemicals and treatment infrastructure are not separately modelled. These are illustrative coefficients, not plant data." .
<https://w3id.org/cerise-see/examples/pv-lci#scenario-background-water-deionised-water-balance-according-to-moek-2013-at-plant-cn-m-watr> dcterms:description "Scenario coefficient per one kg of water, deionised, water balance according to MoeK 2013, at plant. Assume 1000 kg water/m3, EUR 2/m3 for water supply and 0.005 MJ electricity/kg for deionisation. Thus 1 kg requires EUR 0.002 water service and 0.005 MJ electricity. The German monetary water sector is a geographic proxy for Chinese water because the Chinese offering has no published provider URI; Chinese electricity is used. Resins, chemicals and treatment infrastructure are not separately modelled. These are illustrative coefficients, not plant data." .
<https://w3id.org/cerise-see/examples/pv-lci#scenario-reference-water-deionised-water-balance-according-to-moek-2013-at-plant-cn> dcterms:description "One original-unit service or product is supplied. Assume 1000 kg water/m3, EUR 2/m3 for water supply and 0.005 MJ electricity/kg for deionisation. Thus 1 kg requires EUR 0.002 water service and 0.005 MJ electricity. The German monetary water sector is a geographic proxy for Chinese water because the Chinese offering has no published provider URI; Chinese electricity is used. Resins, chemicals and treatment infrastructure are not separately modelled. These are illustrative coefficients, not plant data." .
